  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "#Build a Game Loop with AI\r\n\r\nYou're a Game Engineer building a Minecraft-style dungeon loot system. The game is fully built except for one thing: the while loop that keeps the player opening chests until they find a diamond. That's your job — but you don't have to write it alone. You'll use AI Tutor as your coding partner.\r\n\r\n**What's supposed to happen:** The player opens chests over and over. Each time they open the chest, it reveals a random item — common stuff like bone and string, uncommon items like iron and gold, and rarely, a diamond. The loop keeps opening the chest while a diamond has not been found yet. When the diamond appears, the loop stops and the victory screen shows.\r\n\r\n**Your job:**\r\n\r\n:::details [**1. Plan your prompt**]\r\nBefore you talk to AI Tutor, fill in the ROPE Plan in `prompt.md`\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [**2. Prompt AI Tutor**]\r\nUse your ROPE plan to write a clear prompt. Make sure to tell AI Tutor:\r\n- what loop you need\r\n- what helper functions are available (see comments in `script.js`)\r\n- what the loop should stop on\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [**3. Verify before you ship**]\r\nAI Tutor will give you code. Don't accept it blindly! Run the Debugging Checklist on it.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [**4. Test it**]\r\nRun the game and watch what happens. If the dungeon collapses, your loop has a bug! Diagnose it before asking AI Tutor to fix it.\r\n:::",
